Keep the Qwen3.5 vision tower in pinned host RAM (CUDA UVA) instead of VRAM.

vLLM's --cpu-offload-params only reaches modules built through make_layers();
Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration builds self.visual directly, so
`--cpu-offload-params visual` matches nothing and the ViT lands on the GPU.
With QWEN3_5_VISION_UVA=1 this wraps self.visual in a private UVAOffloader
(the --cpu-offload-gb mechanism: pinned host copy + UVA view, marked
_vllm_is_uva_offloaded so process_weights_after_loading leaves it there).
The global offloader stays a no-op, so no language-model layer is touched.
0.86 GiB of bf16 ViT weights leave the GPU; an image forward reads them over PCIe.
Inert unless the env var is set AND the tower is built (no --language-model-only,
image limit > 0). Only the dense Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration is touched,
not the MoE sibling (identical tower block, disambiguated by the
language_model constructor line in the diff context).

Startup check: the log line "Total CPU offloaded parameters: 0.86 GiB" must
appear exactly once, and Model loading took must stay ~13.97 GiB (<= 14.1).

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/qwen3_5-vision-uva.patch

Written against vLLM 0.27.1, on top of qwen3_5-embed-quant.patch (disjoint hunks).
Reapply after upgrades.

